{number: 102}
{title: In the Garden}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I [Ab] come to the garden alone,
While the dew is still on the [Db] roses,
And the [Eb7] voice I hear falling [Ab] on my ear,
The [Bb7] Son of God dis-[Eb7] closes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And He [Ab] walks with me, and He [Eb7] talks with me,
And He tells me I am His [Ab] own;
And the [C7] joy we [Fm] share as we [Ab] tarry there,
None [Eb7] other has ever [Ab] known.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
He [Ab] speaks, and the sound of His voice,
Is so sweet the birds hush their [Db] singing,
And the [Eb7] melody that He [Ab] gave to me
With-[Bb7] in my heart is [Eb7] ringing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I’d [Ab] stay in the garden with Him
Though the night around me be [Db] falling,
But He [Eb7] bids me go; thru the [Ab] voice of woe
His [Bb7] voice to me is [Eb7] calling.
{end_of_verse}
